We'll configure the Palo Alto side through the GUI, using your existing PAN-OS 11.2.5, `ethernet1/1` WAN interface, and `default` virtual router.

The configuration will use:

- IKEv2 with AES-256-CBC, SHA-256, DH Group 14.
- Route-based IPsec in tunnel mode.
- `tunnel.1` with `10.255.255.1/30`.
- eBGP AS 65001 peering with Cisco AS 65000.
- A dedicated VPN security zone.
- Security policies allowing only the intended inter-site traffic.

These are standard PAN-OS site-to-site VPN components; dynamic routing requires an IP address on the tunnel interface.&#x20;

