## 3. Create the IKE Crypto Profile

Navigate to Network → Network Profiles → IKE Crypto.

Click Add.

Use:

| Field          | Value               |
| -------------- | ------------------- |
| Name           | `IKEV2-CSR-PROFILE` |
| DH Group       | `group14`           |
| Encryption     | `aes-256-cbc`       |
| Authentication | `sha256`            |
| Key Lifetime   | `8 hours`           |

If the interface presents lifetime fields separately, set the lifetime to 8 hours (28,800 seconds).

Click OK.

## 4. Create the IPsec Crypto Profile

Navigate to Network → Network Profiles → IPsec Crypto.

Click Add.

| Field          | Value               |
| -------------- | ------------------- |
| Name           | `IPSEC-CSR-PROFILE` |
| IPsec Protocol | ESP                 |
| Encryption     | AES-256-CBC         |
| Authentication | SHA-256             |
| DH Group       | Group 14            |
| Lifetime       | 1 hour              |

Make sure the PFS/DH Group setting is enabled as Group 14.

Click OK.

These settings match the Cisco transform set and PFS configuration we designed.

## 5. Create the IKE Gateway

Navigate to Network → Network Profiles → IKE Gateways.

Click Add.

### General tab

| Field             | Value           |
| ----------------- | --------------- |
| Name              | `IKE-GW-CSR`    |
| Version           | `IKEv2 only`    |
| Address Type      | IPv4            |
| Interface         | `ethernet1/1`   |
| Local IP Address  | `192.168.1.200` |
| Peer Address Type | IP              |
| Peer Address      | `CISCO_WAN_IP`  |

### Authentication tab

| Field          | Value                   |
| -------------- | ----------------------- |
| Authentication | Pre-Shared Key          |
| Pre-Shared Key | `PaloAltoCiscoVPN2026!` |
| Confirm Key    | Same key                |

### Advanced Options tab

- Enable NAT Traversal if the peers are behind NAT. If they communicate directly without NAT, it is not needed.
- Enable Dead Peer Detection.
- Use the default DPD interval and retry settings initially.
- Leave the local and peer identification fields at their default IP-based behavior if your Cisco identity configuration uses the corresponding WAN IP addresses.

Click OK.

